sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{4})=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cffb8108-0a8b-529c-831d-d01364b7996c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cffb8108-0a8b-529c-831d-d01364b7996c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484792} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aec45a1-2e42-5a0f-985b-263a94020dc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f5d87654-628a-541b-9ab2-cf93106a65ac" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{2 \\pi}{3})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{2 \\pi}{3})=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}.$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d53f014-4a70-5803-8b79-c932cb717d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484844} {:answer/id #uuid "77a9763c-013a-5223-9f90-7999a3c47a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485073} {:answer/id #uuid "8500c686-2515-5751-bd1d-4e17f9147de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485103} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c652c8-dc32-53ee-a293-d90dfad528ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485181} {:answer/id #uuid "b943caa1-1848-5bf8-9949-0cf3348c866e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a9763c-013a-5223-9f90-7999a3c47a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485073} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f4a72e-4cba-5a39-ac58-cf6f7496920a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "111248ff-8060-5580-819b-222a636556c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-5793" :question/problem "Two identical boxes contain marbles. The first box contains two black and four blue marbles. The second box contains one black and five blue marbles. A box is selected at random, and one marble is chosen from the selected box, also at random. If the selected marble is black, what is the probability that it came from the first box?" :question/worked-solution "Let $F$ be the event that the first box is selected, and let $B$ be the event that a randomly selected marble is black. Then, we require $P(F|B),$ which we can compute using Bayes' theorem. \n\n$$\nP(F|B)=\\frac{P(B|F)P(F)}{P(B)}=\\frac{P(B|F)P(F)}{P(B|F)P(F)+P(B|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})}\n$$\n\nNote that ${F}^{′}$ is the event that the second box is selected.\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have the following:\n\n- Since the first box contains two black and four blue marbles, and the second box contains one black and five blue marbles, we have\n\n$$\nP(B|F)=\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P(B|{F}^{′})=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n- Since the box is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=P({F}^{′})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|B) & =\\frac{P(B|F)P(F)}{P(B|F)P(F)+P(B|{F}^{′})P({F}^{′})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6})}{(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
